      story: "In 1993 a short report in Nature said that college students who had just listened to a Mozart sonata did temporarily better on a task involving mentally manipulating shapes. It ballooned into the idea that Mozart makes babies smarter, and the craze went so far that the governor of Georgia asked for funding to give every newborn’s family a classical music CD.",
