      story: "When it was found, the ship was seaworthy and its cargo of alcohol was nearly intact, but the lifeboat was gone, and the captain, his family, and the crew had vanished. What happened to them is still unknown. A young Arthur Conan Doyle wrote a short story based on the case, and details he invented spread as if they were fact.",
